# Build output.
src-tauri/target/

# Regenerated from tauri.conf.json and capabilities/ on every build. Committing
# it means every build shows up as a diff nobody wrote.
src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Installer inputs and output. All of it is BUILT or DOWNLOADED -- ship-windows.sh
# copies the binary and the DLL in, fetches the 115 MB voice pack once, and
# makensis produces the setup. Committing them would put ~270 MB of regenerable
# blobs in the history, and git would carry every version of them forever.
installer/helloim.ai.exe
installer/helloim.ai-Setup.exe
installer/DirectML.dll
# Pre-rename artifact names -- stale build output may still be sitting on disk
# from before the helloim.ai rename; ignore it too rather than let it show up
# as an untracked file waiting to be committed by accident.
installer/NameOS.exe
installer/NameOS-Setup.exe
installer/MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe
installer/vc_redist.x64.exe
installer/vcrt/
installer/tts/
# The updater signature, produced by publish-release.py at release time. It is
# not a secret -- it is just regenerated for every build, and a stale one on
# disk is worse than none.
*.sig
